OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F308A1786054681
OL,3,CGrooming cases to be 'urgently'
OL,4,Cidentified amid early release scheme
OL,5,Cconcerns
OL,7,FAround 5,000 people are expected to be
OL,8,Freleased early under sentencing
OL,9,Fchanges aimed at tackling prison
OL,10,Fovercrowding, down from an initial
OL,11,Festimate of 6,000 after ministers
OL,12,Fexcluded rapists and "serious" child
OL,13,Fsex offenders from the scheme.
OL,15,FHowever, critics have questioned the
OL,16,Fscope of the exemptions after The
OL,17,FTimes reported that some men convicted
OL,18,Fin historical grooming gang cases
OL,19,Fcould still be eligible for early
OL,20,Frelease.
OL,26,@tD@VOUtD@^O]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/7
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,309,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30803
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F308A1786054681
OL,3,CGrooming cases to be 'urgently'
OL,4,Cidentified amid early release scheme
OL,5,Cconcerns
OL,7,FSome of the offences took place before
OL,8,Fchanges to sexual abuse laws in 2003,
OL,9,Fmeaning some perpetrators were
OL,10,Fconvicted of crimes including indecent
OL,11,Fassault, which do not fall under the
OL,12,Fexclusions for the scheme.
OL,14,FConservative leader Kemi Badenoch
OL,15,Fwrote to Andy Burnham on Wednesday
OL,16,Fdemanding clarity over which offences
OL,17,Fwould be eligible for early release,
OL,18,Faccusing the government of "yet
OL,19,Fanother betrayal of victims".
OL,26,@zD@\OU{D@\O]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/7
